      "type": "static modular terrain prototype",
      "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Lanterns Underroot reusable terrain tile atlas for hand-painted 2D side-scrolling platformer. ONE SQUARE1024x1024 image tightly divided into EXACTLY FOUR EQUAL COLUMNS and FOUR EQUAL ROWS, sixteen equal square source cells. No gutters, margin, labels, text, numbers or drawn grid. Each cell contains ONE simple tile module; solid fills touch all connecting cell borders and are not decorative floating islands. Crisp readable orthographic front elevation, no perspective or visible top plane. Restrained painterly texture, muted moss green, earth brown, blue-gray stone and warm amber vocabulary. No buildings, trees, lantern props, characters, UI, scenery, cast shadows, panels or concept board. Transparent background and genuinely alpha-zero outside exposed terrain edges. Designed for64px exports; match adjacent edges. Ancient temple blue-gray slab floor and ceiling modules, warm gray stone, restrained earth staining, tiny moss only upper exposed surfaces. Floors top surfaces, ceilings undersides, corners and caps clear orthographic profiles. Flat solid collision edges extend to cell borders. No loose props. EXACT reading order: Row1: floor left cap; floor middle; floor right cap; isolated floor slab. Row2: ceiling left cap; ceiling middle; ceiling right cap; isolated ceiling slab. Row3: outer top-left corner; outer top-right corner; outer bottom-left corner; outer bottom-right corner. Row4: inner left corner; inner right corner; stone underside middle; stone interior fill.",
